course: dictionary
lesson: 9750
title: A big shop: supermarket
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A supermarket is a big shop where you buy food, drinks and many other things for the home. You take items from the shelves, put them in a trolley or basket, and pay at the checkout.
explain: Shops are places where money and goods change hands, so maths is everywhere in them. You check prices, count the items you buy, work out your change, and compare which product costs less.
explain: «Corner shops often charge more than big supermarkets because they buy smaller amounts.» So the price on the shelf can be different from shop to shop. Compare prices before you decide where to buy, and check any special offers too.
fact: A supermarket is a big shop that sells food, drinks and many other things for the home.
fact: At a supermarket you take items from the shelves, put them in a trolley or basket, and pay at the checkout.
fact: A trolley is a wheeled cage you push round the shop; in the US it is called a cart.
fact: An aisle is the path between the shelves, and a shopping list helps you remember what to buy.
fact: A special offer such as «buy 2, get 1 free» means you get three items but pay for only two.
exercise: What is a supermarket? | A park with swings and a slide | A small house where people sleep | A school for learning maths | *A big shop where you buy food, drinks and many other things
exercise: «Corner shops often charge more than big supermarkets because they buy smaller amounts.» Why do corner shops often charge more? | *They buy smaller amounts | They have no checkout | They are closed at night | They only sell toys
exercise: A sign says «buy 2, get 1 free» for apples at 1 pound each. How much do you pay for three apples? | 3 pounds | *2 pounds | 1 pound | 4 pounds
test: Which word means the wheeled cage you push round the shop? | Aisle | *Trolley | Basket | Checkout
test: Fruit is sold by weight at the supermarket. Which unit is used to weigh it? | *Kilograms | Hours | Litres | Metres
exam: Sam buys 2 kilograms of pears and pays at the checkout. Which word tells you where he paid? | Trolley | Aisle | Shelf | *Checkout
